 "description": "Food-derived medium: metabolizable components of Muscadine grape (Vitis rotundifolia) [Fruits] from FooDB, plus a standard M9 mineral base. Organic components use presence-based uptake bounds; FooDB content retained. Measured compounds with no BiGG exchange are listed under uncovered.",
 "namespace": "bigg",
 "provenance": {
  "source_type": "database",
  "citation": "FooDB v2020-04-07 (Wishart DS et al., foodb.ca). Content sources: PHENOL EXPLORER, USDA.",
  "doi": "",
  "url": "https://foodb.ca/downloads",
  "notes": "Organic components mapped from FooDB compounds to BiGG via InChIKey/name. Mineral base added. Bounds presence-based; foodb_content retained. Unmapped measured compounds kept in uncovered (v2 completeness fix). IMPORTANT: composition values are taken from the archived FooDB 2020-04-07 CSV data release; FooDB's live food page no longer displays this bulk composition, so it will appear empty. Verify individual compounds via the per-component cross-reference links. Underlying content was aggregated by FooDB from USDA / DTU / Phenol Explorer.",
  "data_release": "FooDB 2020-04-07 CSV release (foodb.ca/downloads)",
  "food_record": "https://foodb.ca/foods/FOOD00203",
  "verification": "expert-curated (multi-source food composition; growth-relevant profile completed, FooDB noise removed)",
  "curation_date": "2026-07-17",
  "curation_sources": [
   "USDA FoodData Central FDC 173040 (Grapes, muscadine, raw) - full whole-berry nutrient panel",
   "FooDB FOOD00203",
   "Ector et al., Optimum quality parameters of muscadine grape juices/beverages (sugar & acid means: fructose 5.51%, glucose 5.16%, sucrose 1.89%; malate 0.50%, tartrate 0.26%)",
   "Sandhu & Gu, Fruit Quality/Nutraceutical properties of 58 muscadine varieties (Vitis rotundifolia)",
   "Antioxidants 2021, 10(6):914, doi:10.3390/antiox10060914 (organic-acid profile; malate+tartrate ~90% at ripeness)",
   "Foods 2021, 10(5):1101, doi:10.3390/foods10051101 (juice tartaric 2.6-4.8 g/L)",
   "Lamikanra O. 1997, free amino acids of Noble muscadine, PMID 10606539"
  ],
  "curation_notes": "Dominant carbon/energy sources are D-glucose and D-fructose (~3.7-3.9 g/100g each) plus the previously-missing organic acids malic (~0.50 g/100g) and tartaric (~0.26 g/100g); sucrose is minor. Muscadine is distinctively high in manganese, dietary fiber, and skin phenolics (ellagic acid, resveratrol). Retinol was removed as an implausible animal vitamer (carotenoids substituted); the USDA riboflavin figure (1.5 mg) is a known implausible outlier and was down-corrected to the grape-family referenc",
  "curation_added": [
   "malic acid (dominant organic acid, ~0.50 g/100g)",
   "tartaric acid (~0.26 g/100g)",
   "citric acid (trace)",
   "quantitative individual sugar amounts (glucose 3.67, fructose 3.92, sucrose 0.57 g/100g)",
   "total protein + free amino acid profile (alanine/histidine/arginine)",
   "quantitative minerals (K, Ca, Mg, P, Na, Fe, Zn, Cu, Mn)",
   "vitamin C, riboflavin, folate amounts",
   "dietary fiber, total fat, water",
   "lutein+zeaxanthin"
  ],
  "curation_removed": [
   {
    "name": "Retinol",
    "reason": "Preformed retinol is an animal-derived vitamer; plants/grapes contain provitamin-A carotenoids (beta-carotene) not retinol. FooDB artifact; vitamin-A activity is captured by the carotenoids instead."
   },
   {
    "name": "CO2 CO2",
    "reason": "Metabolic-model exchange/gas species, not a food-composition nutrient."
   },
   {
    "name": "O2 O2",
    "reason": "Metabolic-model exchange/gas species, not a food nutrient."
   },
   {
    "name": "H+",
    "reason": "Proton/pH model artifact, not a quantifiable food nutrient."
   },
   {
    "name": "Fe2+ mitochondria",
    "reason": "Model compartment-tagged duplicate of iron; consolidated into a single 'iron' entry."
   },
   {
    "name": "Iron (Fe3+)",
    "reason": "Redox/species-tagged duplicate of iron; consolidated into a single 'iron' entry."
   },
   {
    "name": "Co2+",
    "reason": "Cobalt: not measured in the USDA muscadine record and not a defining nutrient; generic FooDB trace-mineral placeholder."
   },
   {
    "name": "Nickel",
    "reason": "Non-nutritive trace element, not a measured muscadine nutrient; FooDB generic-mineral padding."
   },
   {
    "name": "Molybdate",
    "reason": "Molybdenum trace element, unmeasured in muscadine; generic FooDB placeholder, not growth-defining."
   }
  ],
